    {
      "id": "UgzUdcd4jLYzEOgJx1Z4AaABAg",
      "author": "@MrCuriousEN",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/jFLCjrN9PuSxu4OhWWfXyG4tIKu3oiUYe0h2sgt4_quh7yyHiSXJfmtG7GV5RMrQKku4qSI6Eg=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "What makes Tristan da Cunha so remarkable is that its isolation is both its greatest protection and its greatest vulnerability. 🌊 With no airport, limited medical access, and supplies dependent on the sea, the community survives through trust, cooperation, and careful use of local resources. The fact that residents chose to return after the volcanic evacuation shows that home is not always where life is easiest, but where identity and belonging are strongest.",
